alice gap probes
================

programs in this directory exercise alice opcodes that hit
evaluator-level gaps in goruby. they're NOT vendored as fixtures
under esolang_tests/alice/ because they fail under goruby today --
they exist as concrete reproducers so the gap_probes_test suite
can confirm the current failure mode and flip to success when
the underlying support lands.

programs
--------

gap_prime.alice -- `2co@`
  push 2; `c` (prime_factors) decomposes 2 into [[2,1]] and pushes
  2; `o` (raw_output) writes byte 2; `@` terminates. mri output:
  one byte 0x02. goruby raises NameError on Prime (the prime
  stdlib is `require`-stubbed but the constant doesn't exist).

opcodes that hit other gaps but can't be reduced to a one-liner
without a tutorial-length alice program:

- Ordinal `x` (permute) + Ordinal `,` (permute_stack) -- both
  route through stable_sort_by which uses sort_by.with_index.
  hits the Enumerator-chaining gap. needs an ordinal-mode entry
  (`/` or `\`) plus a couple of values on the stack.

- Date, force_encoding/scrub, per-string encoding: not reachable
  via alice opcodes -- they're meta-features of the host ruby
  interpreter, not surfaced through alice itself.

see also: evaluator/gap_probes_test.go for direct ruby-level pins
of each gap.
